  Roof: 1307 TFLOP/s bf16 (Matrix-Core), 5300 GB/s HBM3.
  NB: the working set (68-560 KB for these shapes) is L2-resident
      after warmup, so the kernel is NOT HBM-bandwidth-bound -- the
      binding constraint at decode (bs=1, split=1) is OCCUPANCY: the
      grid is ONE wavefront (one of MI300A's 228 CUs). split_kv
      (below) distributes the page range across more CUs and gives
      near-linear speedup; batch scaling is free parallelism up to
      ~228 batches. The follow-on tiled-key/MFMA the kernel's
      docstring references raises occupancy AND moves toward the
      compute roof.

=== split_kv sweep (bs=1 H=32 D=128 B=64 mt=64 nb=64, max_seq_len=4096, 228 CUs) ===
  dsa_topk_logits_split_for(1, 4096, 64) = 64  (recommended)
   split   us(min)   us(med)      GB/s   speedup
       1    1159.7    1169.7       0.5      1.0x
       2     663.8     682.7       0.8      1.7x
       4     465.3     474.9       1.2      2.5x
       8     324.2     328.3       1.7      3.6x
      16     255.6     268.0       2.1      4.4x
      32     212.7     214.4       2.6      5.5x
      64     197.5     200.2       2.8      5.8x
  (split_kv is perf-only and grouping-independent -- the
        reference logit is identical across splits; see
        test_dsa_topk_correct.hip case split=2. Max split
        here is ceildiv(max_seq_len,B)=64. The integrator
        should set split_kv = min(ceildiv(max_seq_len,B),
        CUs/batch_size) -- see dsa.hpp::dsa_topk_logits_split_for.)

=== hip::dsa_topk_logits variant comparison (bs=1 H=32 D=128 B=64 max_seq_len=512, 228 CUs) ===
     var   us(min)   us(med)   vs fp32
    auto     299.4     300.8     1.00x
    fp32    2696.6    2698.7     1.00x
    fp8q    4212.6    4218.6     0.64x
    mfma     298.9     300.4     8.98x
  (auto dispatches mfma here -- the SMALLEST-variant + Matrix-Core path.
   fp32-Q stages Q as fp32 once (49,536 B),
   fp8-Q stages Q raw + dequants on the fly (41,472 B),
   mfma   stages Q transposed bf16 once + bf16 K-tile (16,768 B).
   See dsa.hpp::dsa_topk_logits_fits_lds{,_fp8q,_mfma}.)

